From 38ade7f947cb09c550c2bce077286e467c7fed8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:19:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dspark: simplify copy preparation stream ordering

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
On top of: 5f926df6d3126266a9c88c82c06544060008c33c (C40)

Drop the unproven side-stream preparation/readiness machinery. Run the
unchanged fused match/allocation before DSpark on the current model stream,
then attach the existing asynchronous allocation delivery before DSpark.
FIFO ordering replaces the extra readiness event and join. This is an
explicit simplification, with no serving speedup claim.

Keep the allocation ring and per-slot D2H completion events. For the frozen
PP=1 async profile, two in-flight outputs and get_output completion before
queue credit returns protect the three-slot ring across wrap. Preserve the
fused copy kernels, integer/float copy-state policy, default enablement,
safe capture/decode envelope and inactive top-k scratch-read guard.

Quality: proposals and allocation values must remain identical; delayed
copies must finish before a slot is reused. Replace the side-stream test
with current-stream equivalence and add delayed async ring-wrap coverage
under the enforced two-output bound. No new configuration or fallback.

Tests: five source-only controls, Python 3.12 parse, whitespace and both
C40 offline profile doctors passed. CUDA regressions were authored but not
executed here. Full Linux/image/release gates and both serving boots remain
required; no performance or GPU claim is established by source inspection.

Upstream status: local follow-on patch; not submitted.
